{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>El, Elohim of the spirits.</b> Knower of thoughts — Your measure is not like the measure of flesh and blood: a king of flesh and blood, when part of his province rebels against him, does not know who the sinner is; therefore when he is angry he exacts punishment from all of them. But You — before You all thoughts are revealed, and You know who the sinner is (ibid.)." "<b>One man.</b> He alone is the sinner, yet You are angry with the whole congregation. Said the Holy One, blessed be He: you have spoken well — I know, and I make known, who sinned and who did not sin (ibid.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:18.750996379Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}